ce galore  a lot of blood and loads and loads of  zombies sums up high school of the dead  pretty well  in high school of the dead japan gets  thrown into total chaos overnight with  the start of a zombie apocalypse as the  school gets overrun  our protagonist takashi is forced to  escape with rey the girlfriend of his  friend that he had to unfortunately  execute  what awaits them outside is a society  that's been taken over by the living  dead  thankfully they have allies on their  side joining them is a band of other  student survivors but will their ragtag  group have what it takes to survive this  nightmare one look at the opening and  the poster can pretty much give you an  idea of what to expect now as i said  before the show  is fan service galore but it's also  filled with some nice  action sequences and a genuinely  interesting setting and world it can be  quite mindless in its approach in how it  throws guns and fan service at you but  if you're someone who's in for those  this show will definitely tickle your  fancy  [Applause]  next up is a movie from the year 2000  vampire hunter d  bloodlust if you know it got a movie at  the start of the millennium  and it didn't disappoint the story  revolves around the titular d  a renowned vampire hunter born of the  holy union between  vampire and human his next task has him  on a rescue mission to save the young  noblewoman  charlotte elborn the bounty for his task  is huge and the hunt is on  even with mysterious forces acting in  the background this rescue mission also  seems to be more than it looks at first  glance and perhaps  d has accepted a quest that even a  hunter like him can't handle  vampire hunter d bloodlust is a gripping  movie and i found myself enjoying  every single bit of it now at first  glance it gave me some van helsing and  castlevania vibes i'd say that my first  impressions aren't that far off actually  but the movie still has its unique  points especially in the character  development 